    {
      "id": "yCnT",
      "code_hash": "a8af7dc0d3029782a8e02b74a19d0330",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[50, {\"page\": 1, \"per_page\": 50, \"total\": 351, \"pages\": 8, \"has_next\": true, \"has_prev\": false}]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wlCL",
      "code_hash": "f08188965e2ca3d6b7bae9b82363bb02",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Why a server sends pages.</strong> It answers many people at once, so it limits what one request can cost it. The course shop has more than 15,000 orders behind <code>/shop/orders</code>, with a few more every day, and one reply holding all of them would be slow to send and slow to read. You can ask for bigger pages up to a limit, and past it the server refuses.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "kqZH",
      "code_hash": "c7fc10556c32764f544faf48140c6d25",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[422, {\"detail\": [{\"type\": \"less_than_equal\", \"loc\": [\"query\", \"per_page\"], \"msg\": \"Input should be less than or equal to 100\", \"input\": \"500\", \"ctx\": {\"le\": 100}}]}]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wAgl",
      "code_hash": "456896db175c75dd58608079c2c68df5",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>422</strong> means the request had the right shape and a value the server will not accept. Its reply names the limit.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">So reading everything takes one request per page. <code>get_page</code> asks for one page. <code>per_page=100</code> in its brackets is a <strong>default</strong>: <code>get_page(2)</code> uses 100, and <code>get_page(2, 20)</code> uses 20. The server's parameters have defaults too, which is why leaving out <code>page</code> gave page 1.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "rEll",
      "code_hash": "6faf21dd04d541a6216521c2c7181fe4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
